    "sourceDiscrepancies": [
      "Grid 3 key heading calls this the third cosmic speed and its restated question refers to Earth, while its derivation and the final question concern speed relative to the Sun.",
      "Grid 4 and Grid 7 keys use K for gravitation, while the final question uses G. Grid 4 prose refers to Figure 2 but the solution diagram caption is Fig. 1.",
      "Grid 2 key prints 0.0098 rad and 33.7 arcmin; these printed numbers and its sunrise/sunset wording are retained.",
      "Grid 7 key adds a permanent Earth-facing orientation, says three suspended balls while treating four, drops m in several intermediate b formulas, and prints negative then positive final c tension. These printed forms remain unchanged.",
      "Grid 9 variant setup prints 348000 km but its numerical calculation uses 384000 km. The final question prints 384000 km and requests 50% of the Sun’s magnitude instead of equal brightness.",
      "Grid 6 diagram overlays the numerical derivation in the original PDF. The underlying original PDF text objects were read directly: d=r alpha, 32 arcmin/9.54, 3.35 arcmin, 0.00097 rad and 0.001 rad. This supplied text is restored natively; no computed replacement has been added."
